    "body": "@andypaicu Not being extremely familiar with CSP, how do expect the spec text to play out? As far as I can tell, https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#initialize-document-csp requires a request/response, which `document.open` doesn't have. We could certainly do something like this directly in document open steps:\r\n\r\n> 1. Set _document_'s [CSP list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-document-csp-list) to an empty [CSP list](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#csp-list).\r\n> 1. For each _policy_ in _entryDocument_'s [CSP list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-document-csp-list), insert a copy of _policy_ into _document_’s [CSP list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-document-csp-list).\r\n\r\nBut it seems wrong, as it doesn't run the [initialization](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#directive-initialization) steps for CSP directives, which [initialize a `Document`'s CSP list](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#initialize-document-csp) does. But that's a bit troublesome, as initialization steps also take a _response_.\r\n\r\nPlease advise.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
