    "updated_at": "2019-06-19T11:59:52Z",
    "body": "IMO we should probably do something like this:\r\n\r\n1) Add another initialize-type hook (`initialize-document-csp-from-document`, name WIP) that takes a `target` (document) and a `source` (document)\r\n2) Do something like steps 2 and 3 of [initialize-document-csp](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#initialize-document-csp) to copy the policies and initialize directives\r\n3) Remove the `response` paramater from the [initialize](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#directive-initialization) directive algorithm, or make it optional. I am unaware of any directive that actually uses this.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
